 would record at the brookfield public  library  obviously with covid19 from march of  2020 onward  we haven't been able to hold these  sessions and then i realized i could  keep on doing these by  recording them here in our apartment  and you know doing a video premiere for  about an hour and a half  talking about the particular author and  text and then we would do  a video conferencing session that's a  little bit more intimate  and a little bit more directly engaging  for people who are really into that  particular author  so we're going to continue on with this  for 2021  and we're going to start out online and  then eventually we might be able to move  to face to face we'll see what  actually ends up happening i i don't  know how this is going to work out you  know maybe with a vaccine we'll be able  to start  meeting at the library sometime during  the year or we might just stay  online for the entire time so that is  the series let me tell you who we've  already got  lined up so in january we are going to  be doing  somebody that has been requested quite a  few times and i had scheduled before  uh liu tsi shin the remembrance of  earth's past  trilogy which is is quite good in  february we're going to be returning to  philip k  dick and we're going to be looking at  novels  and also some short stories that have to  do with colonization  of the solar system and with themes of  insanity and sanity there's a lot to  play out in there so obviously like you  know three stigmata of palmer  eldritch we might put in maze of death  even though that's outside of the solar  system  but but some of the other ones as well  like martian time slip  then in march we're going to be reading  some big thick books  our scott backers prince of nothing  trilogy we're not going to try to  attempt to do the entire seven  volumes so far of the second apocalypse  series that the prince of nothing  trilogy is the first three books in each  of them is  is pretty dense and backer is a very  philosophical author  so we're going to be going through those  in  april we're going to pick up uh margaret  atwood's gilead dystopia  so her recent novel um the you know  handmaid's tale and and maybe a few  things  in between in may we're going to be  returning to philip jose  farmer who we did with the river world  series in the past  and we're going to be looking at the  world of tears  novels which are actually earlier than  the river world ones  very interesting stuff we might get in  the seventh  one which i'm not going to tell you too  much about here but it's it's kind of a  meta novel in some ways in june  we're going to return to somebody that  we started out talking about in the very  first year of the series  actually in the very first few months of  the series a van vock one of my  favorite authors from my my childhood  and we're going to be looking at his  weapon maker series  of novels maybe smuggling in a few other  things as well  in july we're going to be returning  again to octavia butler  we did our xenogenesis stuff in in the  past we're going to be looking at the  parable  series now in august  fan requested jg ballard we're going to  be looking at some of his modern  dystopias  and seeing if we can put together a  coherent narrative world maybe yes  maybe no we'll see what happens and then  finally in september  neil stephenson's anathem uh novel this  the  the single big thick um you know  really long enough to wrap our heads  around philosophical  novel by by that author so you notice  what we haven't talked about there  october november december that's up to  you  you are going to be providing  suggestions  in comments and then i'll take the ones  that have the most  um you know repeated calls for those as  comments on this video  and i will um  come up with the top six then we'll have  a vote towards the end of this month  and that will determine who will be  adding  in october november december and we  might actually be meeting face-to-face  by then who knows uh  you know we can we can hope for things  so uh pick  your favorite uh author who i haven't  covered  uh and you might want to take a look at  the series who we've already gone  through and what what particular  narrative world so you're not repeating  yourself so pick an author that you'd  like  me to take on write it in a comment  remember one one author per comment  and if you can say what narrative uh  series or world you want me to focus on  right because some authors have a number  of different  narrative worlds so you know try to be  as specific as possible  this will be a lot of fun i always like  to see what sort of feedback  i get from followers and fans and people  interested in speculative fiction i will  say this is  to sort of close us i have really  benefited  from the suggestion of some of the uh  people  who came to the original talks and would  would you know suggest people to me  year after year after year and from  people  on the internet who watch the various  talks and and  during these voting sessions were like  hey i want you to do this i want you to  do this  there's a lot of thinkers like for  example r scott backer  hadn't read him came up year after year  after year  got around to reading him was blown away  by how how cool the stuff that he was  doing was  all sorts of examples like like that so  make your suggestions  and if there's enough other people  sharing your suggestions you're going to  see that person  go up into the top six and then we'll  vote for  the top three after that  [Music]  you

